THE STATUS THAT IS GONE

`us-proxy` meant "advertising reach, never service area", and three independent
guards enforced that no market carrying it could hold a page, enter areaServed,
or be classified above FUTURE. That was the correct architecture for a company
with no United States position, and every line of it was load-bearing.

The owner confirmed cross-border licensing and crew work authorization on
2026-09-10. The status is gone from the type, from worthiness, from the
opportunity model, from the allocation guard, from the API descriptions, from
llms.txt, from ai.txt and from the corridor copy. Twenty-six western New York
municipalities are now service areas on exactly the same terms as every Ontario
one: a page, real local content, a dated confirmation, a sitemap entry,
areaServed, a markdown twin, an API record and corridor membership.

THE LINE THAT DID NOT MOVE

One shop, one showroom, one telephone number, one set of hours, one set of price
bands, one set of reviews — all Toronto. Not one becomes a local United States
fact on any page. A local number is the single most tempting thing to invent on
a page like this and the claim that turns a true service page into a fabricated
presence, so three guards now fail the build on a second address or a
non-Toronto telephone number anywhere in the geography. The 555 exchange is
whitelisted by name, because failing form placeholders teaches the next person
to delete the check rather than the placeholder.

FORTY-FOUR NEW PAGES

Ontario: King Township with King City and Nobleton; Kleinburg and Woodbridge in
Vaughan; Angus Glen, Bayview Glen and Cachet in Markham; The Kingsway; Port
Credit, Lorne Park, Mineola, Clarkson and Sheridan on the Mississauga lakeshore;
and Lincoln, Welland, Thorold and Fort Erie completing the Niagara belt.

New York: Buffalo, Amherst, Williamsville, Clarence, Cheektowaga, Lancaster,
West Seneca, Tonawanda, Kenmore, Grand Island, Orchard Park, Hamburg, East
Aurora, Niagara Falls NY, Lewiston, Wheatfield, North Tonawanda, Lockport,
Rochester, Brighton, Pittsford, Fairport, Victor, Webster, Irondequoit, Greece.
A new corridor, rochester-east, carries the Monroe and Ontario county run.

THE THIN-CONTENT GUARD CAUGHT ELEVEN OF MY OWN PAGES

verify-cities compares every pair of entries and refused eleven where the
housing note was more than half the same vocabulary as another — beamsville
against lincoln at 95%, west-seneca against greece at 63%, niagara-falls-ny
against niagara-falls-on at 65%. Every one was rewritten about its own place:
Beamsville is fruit-farm houses extended three times with three subfloors to
bring into one plane; Lockport is foundations cut into the rock of the
escarpment where the reading is different at the front wall and the back;
Greece is one long build-out of ranches asking for a third finish they may not
have the thickness to give. That guard is the reason these are pages rather than
a directory.

WHAT REPLACED THE 80/20 FLOOR

Rationing American records was only ever a proxy for "do not publish thin
American pages". Now that they are published the real thing is measured
directly: a floor under the local content of every published page, in both
countries, read from the corpus rather than chosen — just under the tightest
shipped page, so it fails a regression without condemning pages that rank.

THE GREEN GATE

scripts/verify-geo-green.mjs, wired into CI. Every other guard checks one
surface; this one checks that they agree, because the failure this repository
has actually shipped is not a broken page but two true-looking pages
contradicting each other. It refuses a published area with no market record, a
market with content and no page, an orphan outside every corridor, a retired
status in shipped code, a hardcoded territory count, and a second address or
telephone. Its own first run reported all thirty-seven districts as orphans
because its reader could not see partOf; the reader was fixed rather than the
check relaxed.

66 guards green, 317 tests, tsc at its 115-error baseline with nothing new.

